 "drafts": [
  "# Weekly Marketing Brief - Week 12\n\nOverall blended performance declined in the latest week, with CPA increasing and ROAS decreasing. We need to address the underperforming TikTok experiment and the blended CPA target miss.\n\n## Last week vs the period\nBlended spend in week 12 was $23,030 [F1], 10.8% higher [F1] than the $20,785.27 [F1] baseline from weeks 1-11. Blended CPA in week 12 was $79.97 [F2], 12.7% higher [F2] than the $70.94 [F2] baseline. Blended ROAS in week 12 was 0.78x [F3], 10.3% lower [F3] than the 0.87x [F3] baseline.\n\n## What the numbers mean\nGoogle Search CPA in week 6 was $202.90 [F4], 222.1% higher [F4] than the $62.99 [F4] baseline. However, Google Ads conversion data for week 6 (Aug 7-13) is invalid due to a broken conversion tag [N1]; the weekly data cannot isolate the affected days, so this record is uncertain.\n\nTikTok spend in weeks 7-12 was $4,787.83 [F5], 66.7% higher [F5] than the $2,872.33 [F5] baseline, reflecting the 1.6x budget increase for the experiment [N2]. The evaluation rule for the TikTok experiment [N2] states that if TikTok CPA is more than 1.5x [N2] Meta's CPA over the test period, it should be cut. The ratio of TikTok CPA to Meta CPA over weeks 7-12 was 1.92x [F9], which is above the 1.5x [N2] threshold.\n\nMeta conversions in weeks 8-12 were 107 [F6], 23.0% higher [F6] than the 87 [F6] baseline. This period includes the brand awareness campaign that went live on Meta the week of Sep 1 [N3]; we should not judge it on direct CPA [N3].\n\nEmail CPA in week 8 was $23.25 [F7], 35.7% higher [F7] than the $17.14 [F7] baseline.\n\nBlended CPA in week 12 was $79.97 [F8], which did not meet the Q3 target of under $65 [N4].\n\n## Decisions needed\nDecision on the TikTok experiment based on the CPA ratio exceeding the threshold.\n\n## Recommended actions\n- Review TikTok campaign performance and consider budget adjustments or pausing the experiment, as its CPA ratio of 1.92x [F9] exceeds the 1.5x [N2] threshold.\n- Investigate the blended CPA increase in week 12 to identify contributing factors and develop a plan to meet the Q3 target of under $65 [N4].\n- Monitor Meta campaign performance, acknowledging the brand awareness campaign's impact on last-click conversions [N3].\n\n## Data caveats\nGoogle Ads conversion data for week 6 (Aug 7-13) is invalid due to a broken conversion tag [N1], affecting Google Search CPA for that week. The weekly data cannot isolate the affected days, making the record uncertain.",
